                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Hello Friends! I am writing a review for this game because i just beat it and there are few reviews for this game. First off, i am reviewing this game, not another version of it, but the steam version. I never played the other versions of the game, but are aware there out there. Now that i got that out of the way, let me get to the nitty gritty of the game. So this is your basic RPG game, which i like, but it is more like the Ys series. You control one character with 2 people in a party. The main hero is the fighter, so keep your eyes on his hps. The second character is the magic user. You will have to watch her mps. She does not die when you run out of mp, but she becomes useless at that point, other than her special attack..rage.\n\nThis rpg also features side quests and hidden chests all over every map. There are also hidden chambers on most maps. I noticed you need to beat the area, then go back later for it to be open. Anyways, here is my pro/con list:\n\nPROS:\n\n-Ys like rpg game where you fight monstes live time.\n-Hidden things all over the game.\n-Casino mini game.\n-Side quests.\n-Controller support.\n-Multiple endings.\n-Crafting and cooking\n\nCONS:\n\n-What little voice acting in the game, which is only on bosses and casino game, is not very good. I have heard worse though.\n-Leveling can be repetitious at some times, so take your time.\n\nI really liked playing the game. It reminded me of older rpg's similiar to the ys series, which btw, you can also find on steam. I do recommend this game if you like rpg's. Anyways, thank you for reading my review. Have fun gaming!",
